## **SOLID PRINCIPLES ENFORCEMENT**

### **Single Responsibility Principle (SRP)**
- **Rule**: Each class/function has one reason to change
- **Implementation**: One responsibility per unit of code

```swift
// ✅ GOOD: Single responsibility
struct UserValidator {
    func validate(_ user: User) -> ValidationResult {
        // Only validates users
    }
}

struct UserRepository {
    func save(_ user: User) -> Result<Void, SaveError> {
        // Only handles user persistence
    }
}

struct UserNotifier {
    func notifyCreated(_ user: User) -> Result<Void, NotificationError> {
        // Only handles notifications
    }
}
```

### **Open/Closed Principle (OCP)**
- **Rule**: Open for extension, closed for modification
- **Implementation**: Use protocols and composition

```swift
// ✅ GOOD: Extensible without modification
protocol PaymentProcessor {
    func process(_ payment: Payment) -> Result<Receipt, PaymentError>
}

struct CreditCardProcessor: PaymentProcessor {
    func process(_ payment: Payment) -> Result<Receipt, PaymentError> {
        // Credit card specific logic
    }
}

struct PayPalProcessor: PaymentProcessor {
    func process(_ payment: Payment) -> Result<Receipt, PaymentError> {
        // PayPal specific logic
    }
}
```

### **Liskov Substitution Principle (LSP)**
- **Rule**: Derived classes must be substitutable for base classes
- **Implementation**: Consistent contracts and behavior

### **Interface Segregation Principle (ISP)**
- **Rule**: Clients shouldn't depend on interfaces they don't use
- **Implementation**: Small, focused protocols

```swift
// ✅ GOOD: Focused protocols
protocol Readable {
    func read() -> Data
}

protocol Writable {
    func write(_ data: Data) -> Result<Void, WriteError>
}

// ❌ BAD: Fat interface
protocol FileHandler {
    func read() -> Data
    func write(_ data: Data) -> Result<Void, WriteError>
    func compress() -> Data
    func encrypt() -> Data
    func backup() -> Result<Void, BackupError>
}
```

### **Dependency Inversion Principle (DIP)**
- **Rule**: Depend on abstractions, not concretions
- **Implementation**: Inject dependencies through protocols

```swift
// ✅ GOOD: Depends on abstraction
struct UserService {
    private let repository: UserRepositoryProtocol
    private let validator: UserValidatorProtocol

    init(repository: UserRepositoryProtocol, validator: UserValidatorProtocol) {
        self.repository = repository
        self.validator = validator
    }
}
```

