## **DRY PRINCIPLE ENFORCEMENT**

### **Don't Repeat Yourself**
- **Rule**: Every piece of knowledge has single representation
- **Implementation**: Extract common logic, use composition

```swift
// ✅ GOOD: Extracted common validation
struct ValidationHelper {
    static func validateEmail(_ email: String) -> Bool {
        return email.contains("@") && email.contains(".")
    }

    static func validateNonEmpty(_ value: String) -> Bool {
        return !value.trimmingCharacters(in: .whitespaces).isEmpty
    }
}

// Usage in multiple places
func validateUser(_ user: User) -> ValidationResult {
    guard ValidationHelper.validateNonEmpty(user.name) else {
        return .invalid(.emptyName)
    }
    guard ValidationHelper.validateEmail(user.email) else {
        return .invalid(.invalidEmail)
    }

    return .valid
}
```

