## **ENFORCEMENT CHECKLIST**

### **Function Quality Gates**
- [ ] Maximum 3 levels of indentation
- [ ] Maximum 3 parameters
- [ ] Single, clear purpose
- [ ] Early returns for failures
- [ ] Success return at the end
- [ ] No else statements used
- [ ] All primitives wrapped in value objects
- [ ] One dot per line (no method chaining)
- [ ] No abbreviations in names
- [ ] Methods under 5 lines
- [ ] Follows SOLID principles
- [ ] No code duplication (DRY)
- [ ] Simple solution chosen (KISS)

### **Architecture Quality Gates**
- [ ] Clear layer separation
- [ ] Dependencies point inward
- [ ] Protocols used for abstraction
- [ ] Single responsibility per class/struct
- [ ] Maximum 2 instance variables per class
- [ ] Collections wrapped in first-class collection classes
- [ ] Classes under 50 lines
- [ ] Packages under 10 files
- [ ] Composition over inheritance
- [ ] Testable design

---

## **VIOLATION CONSEQUENCES**

### **Function Complexity Violations**
- **>3 Indents**: Extract nested logic into separate functions
- **>3 Parameters**: Create parameter objects or use dependency injection
- **Multiple Purposes**: Split into single-purpose functions

### **Architecture Violations**
- **Dependency Direction**: Refactor to use dependency inversion
- **Layer Mixing**: Separate concerns into appropriate layers
- **Code Duplication**: Extract common logic into shared utilities

